# HW-022 - the SHIPPING demo (overlay-audio.conf), on hardware, after the ES8311
# rewrite. 2026-07-12, COM35 (3rd StickS3, MAC 98:88:e0:0e:dc:64). PASS.
#
# WHY THIS RUN EXISTS. HW-019 and HW-021 flashed the sweep and the stress images. The
# app's own audio paths -- beep, the live mic meter, record and playback -- are reached
# only by navigating to the REC page with the buttons, so NONE of them had run since the
# driver was rewritten. And audio_slab_ok(), the guard I inserted into all four of them,
# had therefore never executed on hardware even once. If I had inverted its condition,
# audio would have been silently dead and every test I ran -- 29 ztests, CI 13/13,
# HW-019, HW-020, HW-021 -- would still have been green.
#
# RESULT: record -> playback works, twice, on two different clips.
#
#   REC start: up to 5000 ms, speak now
#   REC done: 448 ms peak_rms=5210 restarts=1     <- real audio off the microphone
#   PLAY start: 448 ms gain_q8=1024
#   PLAY done                                      <- and again, replayed twice
#   REC done: 2560 ms peak_rms=4343 restarts=1
#   PLAY done
#
#   audio_slab_ok() ran and passed every time. Zero refusals.
#
# TWO THINGS I WILL NOT DRESS UP.
#
# 1. The device rebooted once mid-capture (uptime 103657 -> 399). There is NO signature
#    of a software fault: a Zephyr fatal error prints ">>> ZEPHYR FATAL ERROR" and
#    "Halting system", and this log has neither -- the last line before the gap is a
#    normal `alive` line. What it does have is the monitor's own
#    "ClearCommError failed (PermissionError)" and "Waiting for the device to
#    reconnect", i.e. the USB device disappeared. That is what the LEFT button (the
#    M5PM1 power key) does. I cannot prove which from this log, and I am not going to
#    claim I can. Record -> playback worked before the reboot and again after it; a
#    fault would reproduce, not fire once.
#
# 2. restarts=1, on every recording. It is NOT a regression: the ORIGINAL #14 hardware
#    verification (before any of this work) reads "REC done: 5000 ms peak_rms=684
#    restarts=1" -- the same. The cause is a break in do_record()'s inner loop that
#    logged NOTHING, so a session that died and restarted looked like a session that
#    just worked. That silence is now fixed (LOG_WRN with the errno); the next run will
#    say why. The break has been in main since c84e8d3.
#
